/-!
# First cohomology on the blowup of a regular local surface

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a regular local ring of dimension two and let `X ⟶ Spec(A)` be the blowup of
`Spec(A)` in `𝔪`. Then `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0`, and consequently `H¹(X, ℱ) = 0` for every
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module generated by global sections.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.isZero_firstCohomology_structureSheaf_blowUp_maximalIdeal`:
  `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0`.
* `Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces.isZero_firstCohomology_of_generatingSections`:
  [Stacks, Tag 0AGS] clause (3) for a globally generated module.

## The argument

The source proves clause (2), `H¹(X, 𝒪_X(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1`, by filtering `𝒪_X(-nE)` and
reading the successive quotients `i_*𝒪_E(t)` off the identification of the exceptional divisor
`E` with `𝐏¹_κ` carrying `𝒪_X(E)|_E` to `𝒪(-1)`, which is part of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ]. The
argument here uses only the other part of that tag, the closed immersion `X ⟶ 𝐏¹_{Spec A}`
(`Stacks.Blowup.exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpec_maximalIdeal`), and proves the case `n = 0`,
which is what clause (3) needs. Write `P = 𝐏¹_{Spec A} = Proj A[T₀, T₁]` and let `j : X ⟶ P` be
the closed immersion. Then

* `H¹(P, 𝒪_P) = 0` is Serre's computation on the projective line,
  `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.isZero_lineCohomology_one_of_neg_one_le` at `d = 0`,
  together with the identification of the zeroth twist with the structure sheaf;
* `H²(P, 𝒢) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `𝒢`, because `P` is covered by its two standard
  charts and has affine diagonal: `Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt` at
  `n = 1`;
* the ideal sheaf sequence `0 ⟶ ℐ_j ⟶ 𝒪_P ⟶ j_*𝒪_X ⟶ 0` of the closed immersion is short
  exact and `ℐ_j` is quasi-coherent, so one degree of its long exact sequence gives
  `H¹(P, j_*𝒪_X) = 0`;
* `j` is affine, so `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = H¹(P, j_*𝒪_X)` by [Stacks, Tag 089W].

Clause (3) then follows as in the source: a presentation `⨁_{i ∈ I} 𝒪_X ⟶ ℱ` by global
generators has quasi-coherent kernel, `H¹` commutes with the direct sum, and `H²` vanishes on
quasi-coherent modules — the last being clause (1) of the same tag,
`AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_cohomology_of_two_le`.

## Implementation notes

The blowup is `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp` of the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf that `𝔪` defines,
the spelling clause (1) of the tag already uses, written out as
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom 𝔪)`. The
closed immersion of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ] is stated for `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec`, `Proj` of the
Rees algebra of `𝔪`; the two blowups are identified over `Spec A` by
`Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_over_iso_blowUpToBase`, and an isomorphism followed by a closed
immersion is again one, so no cohomology has to be transported along it.

Cohomology is the right derived functor of `AlgebraicGeometry.moduleGlobalSections`, which is
`Stacks.Cohomology.sectionsFunctor` at the top open by definition. Degrees appear both as
natural numbers (`CategoryTheory.Functor.rightDerived`) and as integers
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.rightDerivedPlus`); `Stacks.DerivedIndexing.rightDerivedIso` moves
between them, and
`Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_hgroup` moves
between the module-valued spelling and the group-valued one in which the projective-line
vanishing above the dimension is stated.

The quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of the blowup, which the direct-sum step needs,
come from properness of the structure morphism over the affine base.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 089W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XT)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase

universe u

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra
attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

namespace Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces

noncomputable section

open Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology (polyGrading)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange
  (isZero_rightDerivedPlus_one_of_shortExact isZero_rightDerivedPlus_one_of_generatingSections)

/-! ### The two inputs on the projective line -/

/-- Vanishing of the `ℕ`-indexed and of the `ℤ`-indexed right derived functor of the global
sections agree. -/
private theorem isZero_rightDerivedPlus_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} (n : ℕ) (G : X.Modules) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections X).rightDerivedPlus n).obj G) ↔
      IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections X).rightDerived n).obj G) :=
  ⟨fun h => h.of_iso ((Stacks.DerivedIndexing.rightDerivedIso _ n).app G),
    fun h => h.of_iso ((Stacks.DerivedIndexing.rightDerivedIso _ n).app G).symm⟩

/-- `H¹(𝐏¹_R, 𝒪) = 0`: Serre's computation of the cohomology of the twists of the projective
line at `d = 0`, together with the identification of the zeroth twist with the structure
sheaf. -/
@[sga "7 X 2.14" "special case"]
private theorem isZero_firstCohomology_unit_projectiveLine (R : Type u) [CommRing R] :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1))).rightDerived 1).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1)).ringCatSheaf)) :=
  IsZero.of_iso
    (Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.isZero_lineCohomology_one_of_neg_one_le R
      (d := 0) (by norm_num))
    (((moduleGlobalSections (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1))).rightDerived 1).mapIso
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjEulerSequence.twistingSheafZeroIsoUnit
        (polyGrading R 1)).symm)

/-- `H²(𝐏¹_R, 𝒢) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `𝒢`: the projective line is covered by its two
standard charts and has affine diagonal, so its cohomological dimension is one. -/
private theorem isZero_secondCohomology_projectiveLine (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    (G : (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1)).Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent] :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1))).rightDerived 2).obj G) :=
  (Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_hgroup
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 2 G).2
    (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt R 1 G 2 (by omega))

/-! ### The structure sheaf of a closed subscheme of the projective line -/

/-- **`H¹(Y, 𝒪_Y) = 0` for a closed subscheme `Y` of the projective line over a ring.**

The ideal sheaf sequence `0 ⟶ ℐ_j ⟶ 𝒪_P ⟶ j_*𝒪_Y ⟶ 0` is short exact and `ℐ_j` is
quasi-coherent, so `H¹(P, 𝒪_P) = 0` and `H²(P, ℐ_j) = 0` give `H¹(P, j_*𝒪_Y) = 0`; and `j` is
affine, so that group is `H¹(Y, 𝒪_Y)`. -/
@[sga "7 X 2.14" "special case"]
private theorem isZero_firstCohomology_unit_of_isClosedImmersion_projectiveLine
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (j : Y ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1)) [IsClosedImmersion j] :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections Y).rightDerived 1).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf)) := by
  have hqc : (Stacks.Tag0B5PClopenLift.idealShortComplex j).X₁.IsQuasicoherent :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasicoherent_kernel_unitToPushforwardObjUnit j
  have hP : IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1))).rightDerivedPlus 1).obj
      (Stacks.Tag0B5PClopenLift.idealShortComplex j).X₃) := by
    refine isZero_rightDerivedPlus_one_of_shortExact
      (Stacks.Tag0B5PClopenLift.shortExact_idealShortComplex j) ?_ ?_
    · exact (isZero_rightDerivedPlus_iff 1 _).2 (isZero_firstCohomology_unit_projectiveLine R)
    · exact (isZero_rightDerivedPlus_iff 2 _).2
        (isZero_secondCohomology_projectiveLine R _)
  have hP' : IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1))).rightDerived 1).obj
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward j).obj (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf))) :=
    (isZero_rightDerivedPlus_iff 1 _).1 hP
  have hL : IsZero ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars j.appTop.hom).obj
      (((moduleGlobalSections Y).rightDerived 1).obj
        (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf))) :=
    IsZero.of_iso hP'
      (Stacks.Cohomology.AffineComparison.cohomologyIsoPushforward j
        (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf) 1)
  have hs := ModuleCat.subsingleton_of_isZero hL
  rw [ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton]
  exact hs

/-! ### The blowup of a regular local surface -/

/-- The blowup of `Spec A` in the maximal ideal of a regular local ring of dimension two is a
closed subscheme of the projective line over `Spec A`, in the ideal-sheaf spelling of the
blowup.

[Stacks, Tag 0AGQ] gives the closed immersion out of `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec`;
`Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_over_iso_blowUpToBase` identifies that blowup with the one in the ideal
sheaf, and an isomorphism followed by a closed immersion is a closed immersion. -/
private theorem exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUp_projectiveLine
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) :
    ∃ j : AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))) ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1), IsClosedImmersion j := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi, -⟩ := Stacks.Blowup.exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpec_maximalIdeal A hdim
  obtain ⟨ε⟩ := Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_over_iso_blowUpToBase A (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
  refine ⟨((Over.forget _).mapIso ε).inv ≫ i, ?_⟩
  have : IsIso (((Over.forget _).mapIso ε).inv) := inferInstance
  infer_instance

/-- **`H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0` on the blowup of a regular local ring of dimension two at its maximal
ideal.**

This is the case `n = 0` of clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGS], proved from the closed immersion
of the blowup into the projective line over the base rather than from the source's filtration
of the twists along the exceptional divisor. -/
theorem isZero_firstCohomology_structureSheaf_blowUp_maximalIdeal
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))))).rightDerived 1).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
          (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
            (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)))).ringCatSheaf)) := by
  obtain ⟨j, _⟩ := exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUp_projectiveLine A hdim
  exact isZero_firstCohomology_unit_of_isClosedImmersion_projectiveLine j

/-- `H^p` of a quasi-coherent module on the blowup vanishes for `p ≥ 2`, in the module-valued
spelling. This is clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGS],
`AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_cohomology_of_two_le`, read through the comparison of the
group-valued and module-valued sections functors. -/
private theorem isZero_cohomology_two_le_blowUp_maximalIdeal
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2)
    (G : (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)))).Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent]
    (p : ℕ) (hp : 2 ≤ p) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))))).rightDerived p).obj G) :=
  (Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_hgroup
    (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)))).ringCatSheaf ⊤ p G).2
    (AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_cohomology_of_two_le A hdim G p hp)

/-- The structure morphism of the blowup of the spectrum of a regular local ring is proper: the
base is locally Noetherian, so the centre is finitely generated on every affine open. -/
private theorem isProper_blowUpToBase_maximalIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] :
    IsProper (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)))) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_blowUpToBase_of_fg _ fun U =>
    have := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
    Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _

/-- Let `A` be a regular local ring of dimension two and let `X ⟶ Spec(A)` be the blowup of
`Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal. Then `H¹(X, ℱ) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ`
generated by global sections.

The presentation `⨁_{i ∈ σ.I} 𝒪_X ⟶ ℱ` by the generators has quasi-coherent kernel, `H¹`
commutes with the direct sum because `X` is quasi-compact and quasi-separated, `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0`,
and `H²` vanishes on quasi-coherent modules by clause (1) of the same tag. -/
@[stacks 0AGS "clause (3), for a module generated by global sections"]
theorem isZero_firstCohomology_of_generatingSections
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2)
    (F : (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)))).Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (σ : SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections F) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))))).rightDerivedPlus 1).obj F) := by
  have := isProper_blowUpToBase_maximalIdeal A
  have : CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))) : Type u) :=
    QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))))
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))) : Type u) :=
    quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))))
  refine isZero_rightDerivedPlus_one_of_generatingSections F σ ?_ ?_
  · exact (isZero_rightDerivedPlus_iff 1 _).2
      (isZero_firstCohomology_structureSheaf_blowUp_maximalIdeal A hdim)
  · intro G _
    exact (isZero_rightDerivedPlus_iff 2 _).2
      (isZero_cohomology_two_le_blowUp_maximalIdeal A hdim G 2 le_rfl)

end

end Stacks.ResolutionOfSurfaces

end
